<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ehime Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ehime Prefecture is a prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the north-west of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shikoku">Shikoku</a>, with its capital at Matsuyama. It covers the old province of Iyo and was formed in 1873 from prefectures created after the abolition of the domains in 1871, including those of Matsuyama, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uwajima">Uwajima</a> and other former domains. It is known for citrus farming and for the Dogo hot springs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ehime-prefecture.jpg" alt="Ehime Prefecture" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dokudami · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isidutisan20220226_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
